    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8627" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνηλε-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνελεής</span>
			, <i>without pity, unmerciful,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Epit.</u>
				478
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Del.</u>
				106
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Parth.
				14.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Mith.</u>
				38
			</span></i>; poet. acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνηλέα</span> (as if
			from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνηλής</span>) <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				418
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Cyrene</span>); gen. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνηλέος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					1.263
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνηλής</span> is dub. in <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				81
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>An.Ox.</u>
				1.60
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Aff.</u>
					40
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				4.39
			</span></i>.</div>
